---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ModeBadge from '../components/ModeBadge.astro';
import { categories, href, tools } from '../tools';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Tools">
  <a slot="home-link" class="corner corner-tl" href={href()}>All tools</a>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Every tool is labelled with where your file is processed.</p>

    <h2><ModeBadge mode="local" label /></h2>
    <p>The file is opened and processed by JavaScript running in your browser tab. File contents and file names are never sent anywhere: not to our servers, not to analytics, not into URLs or error reports. You can verify this in your browser's developer tools (Network tab) while using a tool. Results are created in memory and downloaded directly.</p>
    <p>Closing or clearing the tool releases our references to your file. This is not a secure-erase guarantee against your browser's memory, operating-system swap, extensions or malware on your device.</p>

    <h2><ModeBadge mode="cloud" label /></h2>
    <p>Some tasks need more computing power than a browser offers. Before each upload you are asked to confirm; that answer is never remembered.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your file is sent over HTTPS directly to our processing service on Google Cloud Run in Belgium (<code>europe-west1</code>).</li>
      <li>It is processed in memory and discarded when the result is returned. No storage bucket, history, or cached result exists.</li>
      <li>We log operational metadata only: time, response status, size and duration. The hosting provider processes connection metadata such as your IP address.</li>
      <li>Your file is not used to train models and is not sent to third-party AI services.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Which tools use the cloud?</h2>
    <table class="tool-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Processing</th></tr></thead>
      {categories.map((c) => (
        <tbody style={`--cat: var(--c-${c.id})`}>
          <tr class="cat-row"><th colspan="2" scope="rowgroup"><Icon name={c.id} />{c.label}</th></tr>
          {tools.filter((t) => t.category === c.id).map((t) => <tr><td>{t.title}</td><td><ModeBadge mode={t.mode} label /></td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      ))}
    </table>

    <h2>GPX background map</h2>
    <p>The GPX map has no background map unless you choose one. If you pick <em>Map</em> or <em>Satellite</em>, map images are loaded from OpenStreetMap or Esri. Those servers then see which area you are viewing and your IP address, as with any website that shows a map. Your GPX file itself is never sent.</p>

    <h2>Stored on your device</h2>
    <p>Only preferences you set (theme, default image format and quality) are stored in your browser's local storage. You can reset them on the <a href="../settings/">settings page</a>. No cookies, no tracking.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { margin-inline: auto; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .tool-table tbody td:first-child { border-left: 3px solid var(--cat); padding-left: 0.75rem; }
  .cat-row th {
    padding: 1.1rem 0.75rem 0.4rem; border-bottom: 0; color: var(--cat);
    font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .cat-row :global(.icon) { margin-right: 0.4rem; vertical-align: -0.2em; }
  .cat-row :global(.icon svg) { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
</style>
